WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.320 --> 00:00:05.360
Researchers at Foundation Site 202 were going
about their day as they would normally, or

00:00:05.360 --> 00:00:08.970
as normal as a day could be in the SCP Foundation.

00:00:08.970 --> 00:00:12.339
If anything, normality was abnormal for them.

00:00:12.339 --> 00:00:17.840
It was a quiet day at Site 202, as it had
been for a few weeks, to the distress of many

00:00:17.840 --> 00:00:20.289
of the researchers stationed at the site.

00:00:20.289 --> 00:00:25.210
No anomalies had breached containment in the
past twenty days, there were no random anomalous

00:00:25.210 --> 00:00:29.759
events to investigate, testing was up to date
for all the anomalies they had contained in

00:00:29.759 --> 00:00:34.370
the past few months, and their leads on potential
anomalies had run dry.

00:00:34.370 --> 00:00:39.220
There was little to do at Site 202, and its
researchers grew restless as the piles and

00:00:39.220 --> 00:00:43.420
piles of boring Foundation paperwork grew
ever taller.

00:00:43.420 --> 00:00:47.670
That was until a fateful day in the Spring
of 1990.

00:00:47.670 --> 00:00:49.890
It was March 22.

00:00:49.890 --> 00:00:53.920
The cold winter weather had still lingered
in the air that day, but it was warming up

00:00:53.920 --> 00:00:56.609
for all the people living around the Site.

00:00:56.609 --> 00:01:01.450
There was word that a school, not too far
from Site 202, was experiencing an event that

00:01:01.450 --> 00:01:07.320
could only be described as potentially catastrophic
to the SCP Foundation’s reality.

00:01:07.320 --> 00:01:12.979
Of the researchers at Site 202, five were
deemed suitable to form a temporary task force.

00:01:12.979 --> 00:01:17.490
The first, Doctor J. Alfred Henry a senior
researcher who was a former member of the

00:01:17.490 --> 00:01:23.659
Mobile Task Force The Mole Rats during the
investigation into SCP-1730, the interdimensional

00:01:23.659 --> 00:01:25.200
Site-13.

00:01:25.200 --> 00:01:29.610
Doctor Henry also brought along his assistant,
researcher Tyler Zeissman.

00:01:29.610 --> 00:01:34.479
The next member was Yavan Olich, who was in
charge of taking care of any living anomalies

00:01:34.479 --> 00:01:37.060
that may be present at the location.

00:01:37.060 --> 00:01:41.579
Another member of this team was Spriggand
Firestarter, a former member of the anomalous

00:01:41.579 --> 00:01:46.939
Group of Interest: The Serpent’s Hand, which
specializes in magic and spell casting.

00:01:46.939 --> 00:01:51.619
This project was overseen by Samantha Strysand,
the director of Site 202.

00:01:51.619 --> 00:01:57.039
The team was not given a normal designation
as most tasks forces are: a greek letter and

00:01:57.039 --> 00:01:58.039
a number.

00:01:58.039 --> 00:02:03.549
Instead, they were called the “Taint Team”
and were in charge of documenting and combating

00:02:03.549 --> 00:02:07.360
any and all parts of reality that were tainted
by the anomaly.

00:02:07.360 --> 00:02:10.830
The team set out for the location of this
potential anomaly.

00:02:10.830 --> 00:02:15.330
Along with their standard-issue firearms and
tactical armor, they were armed with portable

00:02:15.330 --> 00:02:20.180
Scranton Reality Anchors and possibly the
most important part of their arsenal: their

00:02:20.180 --> 00:02:21.550
expertise.

00:02:21.550 --> 00:02:25.921
The location the taint team arrived at was
nothing they were expecting from what they

00:02:25.921 --> 00:02:29.150
had heard about past reality-altering anomalies.

00:02:29.150 --> 00:02:32.150
They were greeted with a single school building.

00:02:32.150 --> 00:02:36.040
It was large in size; more a castle than a
school.

00:02:36.040 --> 00:02:40.850
It was constructed out of red bricks, with
the roofs being slanted and white.

00:02:40.850 --> 00:02:44.370
In the center of the building complex was
a large clock tower.

00:02:44.370 --> 00:02:49.540
The researchers commented on how similar it
looked to a nearby church, and continued inside.

00:02:49.540 --> 00:02:53.520
They moved throughout the school, looking
around for any sign of abnormalities.

00:02:53.520 --> 00:02:58.970
There were three floors and two wings, but
all of them housed no anomaly.

00:02:58.970 --> 00:03:03.320
The portable Scranton Reality Anchors each
member of the taint team held were not picking

00:03:03.320 --> 00:03:06.350
up on any levels of reality instability.

00:03:06.350 --> 00:03:11.400
They were close to calling the investigation
a false-positive and move back to Site 202

00:03:11.400 --> 00:03:16.070
when a faint beeping noise was heard from
all the members of personnel.

00:03:16.070 --> 00:03:19.350
Doctor Olich was the only one not to react
to the sound out of the team.

00:03:19.350 --> 00:03:22.560
“It’s just a meat processing plant,”
he said sternly.

00:03:22.560 --> 00:03:25.180
“There’s nothing in here except empty
rooms and dust.

00:03:25.180 --> 00:03:26.180
Let’s head back.”

00:03:26.180 --> 00:03:28.040
The rest of the team was confused.

00:03:28.040 --> 00:03:30.100
“A meat processing plant?”

00:03:30.100 --> 00:03:33.620
They were all briefed numerous times that
this was a school.

00:03:33.620 --> 00:03:37.440
Olich was the first one to comment that he
recognized the location.

00:03:37.440 --> 00:03:40.450
Was this the reality altering anomaly they
were looking for?

00:03:40.450 --> 00:03:44.280
A school that makes people think it’s a
meat processing plant.

00:03:44.280 --> 00:03:47.520
That wouldn’t be the weirdest anomaly the
Foundation has found.

00:03:47.520 --> 00:03:49.460
One site has a yeti working for them.

00:03:49.460 --> 00:03:51.580
But this, was rather underwhelming.

00:03:51.580 --> 00:03:54.620
“What do you mean a meat processing plant?”

00:03:54.620 --> 00:03:55.620
Inquired Doctor Henry.

00:03:55.620 --> 00:03:59.210
“Whatever, let’s just go,” Olich responded
coldly.

00:03:59.210 --> 00:04:03.300
Doctor Henry stopped him as he turned and
looked to his portable reality anchor.

00:04:03.300 --> 00:04:07.840
There was a rise in Humes on the other side
of the main corridor on the first floor.

00:04:07.840 --> 00:04:10.330
Humes are a unit of reality stability.

00:04:10.330 --> 00:04:14.010
Baseline reality is located at a Hume level
of 0.

00:04:14.010 --> 00:04:18.880
Anything or anyone with a Hume level greater
than that is able to affect reality in various

00:04:18.880 --> 00:04:19.880
ways.

00:04:19.880 --> 00:04:24.100
The team moved slowly to the other side of
this room, once again finding nothing except

00:04:24.100 --> 00:04:26.880
the white drywall and tile flooring of the
building.

00:04:26.880 --> 00:04:31.500
There was one odd element as they approached
this portion, though: a door.

00:04:31.500 --> 00:04:35.730
It was not like any of the heavy steel doors
the team had seen in the building.

00:04:35.730 --> 00:04:39.120
It was wooden, like the one you’d see on
a house.

00:04:39.120 --> 00:04:41.010
The Hume reader skyrocketed.

00:04:41.010 --> 00:04:43.780
It was a number they had never seen before.

00:04:43.780 --> 00:04:45.740
4000 humes.

00:04:45.740 --> 00:04:49.861
After a tense second of looking to each other
on what their next move should be, Doctor

00:04:49.861 --> 00:04:54.850
Henry slowly reached his hand out to the door
and twisted the bronze handle as the rest

00:04:54.850 --> 00:04:56.730
of the team drew their weapons.

00:04:56.730 --> 00:05:00.700
He opened it quickly, finding nothing but
a dusty staircase.

00:05:00.700 --> 00:05:04.600
The Hume reader plummeted back to normal levels
as quickly as it had spiked.

00:05:04.600 --> 00:05:06.600
The team discussed what they should do next.

00:05:06.600 --> 00:05:11.150
They decided to enter the basement level,
which they found was not listed on the floorplan

00:05:11.150 --> 00:05:12.430
of the building.

00:05:12.430 --> 00:05:17.330
Doctor Olich, insisted, however, that he remembered
this meat processing plant having a basement.

00:05:17.330 --> 00:05:21.740
They moved into the dark stairway and slowly
progressed down the stairs.

00:05:21.740 --> 00:05:25.310
It was an oddly short staircase that led to
an oddly small room.

00:05:25.310 --> 00:05:27.470
The team was once again confused.

00:05:27.470 --> 00:05:31.530
Why did the Hume levels hit a record high
if there was nothing but a small boiler and

00:05:31.530 --> 00:05:34.350
a few pipes snaking on the walls?

00:05:34.350 --> 00:05:37.050
Doctor Olich was notably absent from the team.

00:05:37.050 --> 00:05:41.860
After some searching, he was found a bit up
the flight of stairs, frozen in place with

00:05:41.860 --> 00:05:42.860
fear.

00:05:42.860 --> 00:05:44.710
“Yavan,” Doctor Henry called.

00:05:44.710 --> 00:05:45.710
“What’s wrong?”

00:05:45.710 --> 00:05:49.930
There was no response, as Doctor Olich just
stood there frozen in shock.

00:05:49.930 --> 00:05:54.970
Then suddenly the silent doctor began to walk
down the steps almost robotically; his eyes

00:05:54.970 --> 00:05:59.490
were locked on the boiler, but it didn’t
look like anything was wrong with it to the

00:05:59.490 --> 00:06:01.350
eyes of everyone else.

00:06:01.350 --> 00:06:04.890
Doctor Olich entered the room with the rest
of the team and moved towards the boiler.

00:06:04.890 --> 00:06:06.480
“You don’t see it?”

00:06:06.480 --> 00:06:07.480
Olich said.

00:06:07.480 --> 00:06:08.480
“The– the veins.”

00:06:08.480 --> 00:06:10.690
“What are you talking about?”

00:06:10.690 --> 00:06:11.690
Doctor Henry responded.

00:06:11.690 --> 00:06:13.610
“There’s nothing wrong here.”

00:06:13.610 --> 00:06:17.320
Researcher Zeissman moved toward Doctor Olich
in an attempt to calm him down.

00:06:17.320 --> 00:06:21.610
As he approached, Doctor Olich became hostile
and began fighting the researcher.

00:06:21.610 --> 00:06:25.590
The other members of the taint team attempted
to calm and restrain the doctor, but Olich

00:06:25.590 --> 00:06:28.060
thwarted these attempts and moved to a corner.

00:06:28.060 --> 00:06:29.060
“Blood!”

00:06:29.060 --> 00:06:30.060
Olich cried.

00:06:30.060 --> 00:06:31.320
“He wants blood.

00:06:31.320 --> 00:06:32.600
A lot.

00:06:32.600 --> 00:06:33.600
Blood.”

00:06:33.600 --> 00:06:38.291
Doctor Henry began frantically radioing Director
Strysand in an attempt to get more help, but

00:06:38.291 --> 00:06:42.150
as he did, Olich cried out the word Blood
another time.

00:06:42.150 --> 00:06:43.850
A gun shot rang out.

00:06:43.850 --> 00:06:47.770
His body fell to the ground, but his blood
did not.

00:06:47.770 --> 00:06:52.410
The blood of Doctor Olich began flowing up
the walls in a jagged pattern, then began

00:06:52.410 --> 00:06:54.360
to absorb into the concrete.

00:06:54.360 --> 00:06:58.710
Suddenly, the Hume levels spiked in the room,
and the blaring alarms of the portable reality

00:06:58.710 --> 00:07:01.050
anchors were all that could be heard.

00:07:01.050 --> 00:07:06.030
The room switched in appearance, attached
to all four walls on the basement were hundreds

00:07:06.030 --> 00:07:08.490
of long, thick veins.

00:07:08.490 --> 00:07:13.930
They were red and black and purple, and dripped
a syrupy liquid of the same color onto the

00:07:13.930 --> 00:07:14.930
ground.

00:07:14.930 --> 00:07:18.790
There was almost a foot of the liquid in the
room, which the agents had been standing in

00:07:18.790 --> 00:07:20.490
without even knowing it.

00:07:20.490 --> 00:07:23.750
There was a mass slithering towards the corpse
of Doctor Olich.

00:07:23.750 --> 00:07:26.660
It was black and a deep red in color.

00:07:26.660 --> 00:07:30.550
It almost looked like a person, but it didn’t
move or act like one.

00:07:30.550 --> 00:07:35.450
The entity absorbed the body of Doctor Olich
into its central mass and began moving towards

00:07:35.450 --> 00:07:37.630
the remaining members of the taint team.

00:07:37.630 --> 00:07:41.930
The Foundation personnel yelled into their
walkies that they needed to be evacuated immediately.

00:07:41.930 --> 00:07:45.400
They sprinted up the stairs toward the roof
and out of the building.

00:07:45.400 --> 00:07:50.210
Just as they reached the roof top: They heard
a terrifying gutteral rumbling voice mutter

00:07:50.210 --> 00:07:54.070
the word “More.”

00:07:54.070 --> 00:07:58.250
Their reality anchors’ Hume readers then
plummeted back to normal levels.

00:07:58.250 --> 00:08:02.050
And a Foundation helicopter arrived to evacuate
them from the roof top.

00:08:02.050 --> 00:08:06.820
The Foundation would designate this anomaly
as SCP-5633.

00:08:06.820 --> 00:08:10.930
They devised a number of containment procedures
to combat the anomaly.

00:08:10.930 --> 00:08:16.110
Site 202 was to be used as a drainage facility
for the anomaly’s secretions and all personnel

00:08:16.110 --> 00:08:21.990
who enter the basement of SCP-5633 must not
have a phobia of blood.

00:08:21.990 --> 00:08:27.481
As with most anomalies, the SCP Foundation
personnel of Site 202 decided to conduct some

00:08:27.481 --> 00:08:32.280
testing under the belief that SCP-5633 could
speak to them again.

00:08:32.280 --> 00:08:37.650
Blood, used for transfusions at the Foundation,
was transported from Site-17 for the taint

00:08:37.650 --> 00:08:40.630
team to use as bate to attempt an interview.

00:08:40.630 --> 00:08:45.520
It had been over a month since the taint team
had been to SCP-5633.

00:08:45.520 --> 00:08:51.529
They remained with three members despite losing
one to the anomaly, as they were all familiar

00:08:51.529 --> 00:08:53.339
enough with the building.

00:08:53.339 --> 00:08:57.810
Doctor Henry placed down a bag of blood and
readied his reality anchor.

00:08:57.810 --> 00:09:01.880
Immediately the blood was drained out of the
bag and began to flow up the walls of the

00:09:01.880 --> 00:09:02.880
basement.

00:09:02.880 --> 00:09:06.630
As Hume levels spiked, the room revealed its
true form.

00:09:06.630 --> 00:09:08.400
The humanoid entity responded.

00:09:08.400 --> 00:09:13.440
“I AM GLAD YOU KNOW WHAT TO DO.”

00:09:13.440 --> 00:09:15.100
Another bag of blood was placed down.

00:09:15.100 --> 00:09:19.910
“YOU ARE NOW PART OF MY CREATION.”

00:09:19.910 --> 00:09:23.380
It was decided that two bags would be placed
next.

00:09:23.380 --> 00:09:27.680
Doctor Henry believed that more blood would
potentially get a greater result.

00:09:27.680 --> 00:09:31.830
“YOU SHOULD FOLLOW EVERY INSTRUCTION I GIVE
YOU.

00:09:31.830 --> 00:09:39.080
YOU SHOULD GIVE ME BLOOD EACH TIME OR I WILL
STOP GIVING YOU INSTRUCTIONS.”

00:09:39.080 --> 00:09:41.110
Another two bags of blood were placed down.

00:09:41.110 --> 00:09:46.740
But this time no phrase was given from SCP-5633.

00:09:46.740 --> 00:09:49.740
Instead a bundle of papers fell from one of
the veins.

00:09:49.740 --> 00:09:53.330
It depicted the blueprints for Site 202.

00:09:53.330 --> 00:09:58.240
Whether this was a threat or a message, it
did not matter to the personnel at Site 202

00:09:58.240 --> 00:10:00.500
that was overseeing the project.

00:10:00.500 --> 00:10:04.140
They commanded that all of the taint team
were to return to base at once.

00:10:04.140 --> 00:10:09.600
While the SCP Foundation has ways to combat
reality-altering events, they also have methods

00:10:09.600 --> 00:10:12.060
to look into alternate realities.

00:10:12.060 --> 00:10:18.830
As SCP-5633 is one of these reality-bending
anomalies, it was decided a much more in-depth

00:10:18.830 --> 00:10:20.740
investigation was needed.

00:10:20.740 --> 00:10:27.300
It was found that in an alternate timeline,
SCP-5633 was a meat processing plant that

00:10:27.300 --> 00:10:29.810
suffered a reality alteration.

00:10:29.810 --> 00:10:34.649
The taint team, in that reality, had been
trapped in the meat processing plant only

00:10:34.649 --> 00:10:37.930
to fight and destroy SCP-5633.

00:10:37.930 --> 00:10:45.530
Somehow, they were able to disconnect SCP-5633’s
control on them and the meat processing plant,

00:10:45.530 --> 00:10:51.340
then overseeing researchers were able to attach
SCP-5633 to various realities that were different

00:10:51.340 --> 00:10:52.490
from its own.

00:10:52.490 --> 00:10:55.200
It became confused and destroyed itself.

00:10:55.200 --> 00:11:02.270
Did the SCP Foundation of another reality
accidentally send SCP-5633 to this reality?

00:11:02.270 --> 00:11:07.180
It seems that way, so perhaps this version
of the SCP Foundation could contain it by

00:11:07.180 --> 00:11:12.710
sending it to another reality, perhaps one
that it didn’t have power in at all.

00:11:12.710 --> 00:11:16.160
The taint team decided that this was the course
of action they would take.

00:11:16.160 --> 00:11:20.460
They reviewed the file they had recovered
from the servers of an alternate reality,

00:11:20.460 --> 00:11:24.700
finding that blood was the correct sacrifice
to give to SCP-5633.

00:11:24.700 --> 00:11:32.460
There was an issue though, the humanoid entity
within SCP-5633 had been growing larger, along

00:11:32.460 --> 00:11:35.149
with its already intense power.

00:11:35.149 --> 00:11:39.570
Tests were being run on the substance found
in the basement, as Site 202 had been draining

00:11:39.570 --> 00:11:43.300
and pumping it into a disposal and storage
laboratory.

00:11:43.300 --> 00:11:48.980
It was found to be a mixture of blood and
DNA from over 2000 different human sources.

00:11:48.980 --> 00:11:53.740
There was a catastrophic accident with one
of the drainage pipes in Site 202.

00:11:53.740 --> 00:11:58.290
One had been heated to intense temperatures,
causing a potential meltdown of the entire

00:11:58.290 --> 00:11:59.290
site.

00:11:59.290 --> 00:12:03.459
On-Site security and repair teams moved in
swiftly to combat the issue, however, the

00:12:03.459 --> 00:12:08.600
superheating and rapid flooding led to the
pipe bursting from shock, splattering everyone

00:12:08.600 --> 00:12:12.180
in it’s vicinity with SCP-5633’s fluid.

00:12:12.180 --> 00:12:18.040
The fluid acted almost as acid, burning away
armor, clothes, skin, and muscle tissue and

00:12:18.040 --> 00:12:21.000
embedding itself into the bodies of the victims.

00:12:21.000 --> 00:12:25.740
They were immediately placed into temporary
containment, as, at the time, it was unknown

00:12:25.740 --> 00:12:28.850
what would happen when the liquid entered
the bloodstream.

00:12:28.850 --> 00:12:31.399
As always, tests were performed on the wounded.

00:12:31.399 --> 00:12:35.880
They found that the entirety of the DNA of
those who had been victims of the liquid was

00:12:35.880 --> 00:12:41.110
instead reading as SCP-5633’s DNA, not their
own.

00:12:41.110 --> 00:12:43.930
For the time, the victims seemed fine.

00:12:43.930 --> 00:12:49.220
That was until a week later when all the victims
of this event were found dead in their cells

00:12:49.220 --> 00:12:51.780
with cuts on their wrists and throats.

00:12:51.780 --> 00:12:55.260
Logically this would be the most efficient
way to drain the most amount of blood out

00:12:55.260 --> 00:12:58.120
of their bodies in the shortest period of
time.

00:12:58.120 --> 00:13:02.920
The oddest part of this entire ordeal: There
was no blood pooled on the ground whatsoever.

00:13:02.920 --> 00:13:08.790
There were only faintly red trails of blood
up the walls of each cell.

00:13:08.790 --> 00:13:15.279
That same day, SCP-5633 was observed to have
grown over twice in size.

00:13:15.279 --> 00:13:19.420
If the anomaly could affect people who are
not even in the room, what’s preventing

00:13:19.420 --> 00:13:23.399
it from spreading this liquid to all corners
of the Earth and drawing all of the human

00:13:23.399 --> 00:13:25.670
races’ blood into its mass?

00:13:25.670 --> 00:13:31.460
The taint team was given a supply of blood
to draw SCP-5633 out so that reality anchors

00:13:31.460 --> 00:13:35.100
could be placed and it could be sent to another
reality.

00:13:35.100 --> 00:13:39.200
The plan was simple, with Doctor Henry and
Researcher Zeissman placing the blood bags

00:13:39.200 --> 00:13:44.770
down and communicating with the entity, Firestarter
would place down three portable Scranton Reality

00:13:44.770 --> 00:13:47.670
Anchors to contain the entity for a time.

00:13:47.670 --> 00:13:53.520
The taint team journeyed to SCP-5633, this
time accompanied by Director Strysand.

00:13:53.520 --> 00:13:59.440
The site director believed that all the deaths
caused by SCP-5633 were at her hand, as she

00:13:59.440 --> 00:14:02.899
had more than enough time to intervene but
didn’t.

00:14:02.899 --> 00:14:08.529
This time, she was ready to send this anomaly
out of her reality by any means necessary.

00:14:08.529 --> 00:14:12.980
The brick wall of the school had gone from
a nostalgic reminder of elementary school

00:14:12.980 --> 00:14:17.480
to a nightmare of dead colleagues and the
potential death of reality.

00:14:17.480 --> 00:14:23.670
They were careful when they entered, despite
knowing SCP-5633 was located in the basement.

00:14:23.670 --> 00:14:27.839
Everyone on the team was tense but knew they
had a mission in mind.

00:14:27.839 --> 00:14:33.130
They were ready to die in the dark if that
meant everyone could live in the light.

00:14:33.130 --> 00:14:36.750
With a swift hand, Doctor Henry opened the
door to the basement, and the three other

00:14:36.750 --> 00:14:39.120
members of the taint team followed suit.

00:14:39.120 --> 00:14:41.760
The basement once again appeared to be normal.

00:14:41.760 --> 00:14:47.660
The team knew this was a false sense of security
put in place by SCP-5633 so it could coil

00:14:47.660 --> 00:14:51.519
around them and drain their blood so it could
grow in size and power.

00:14:51.519 --> 00:14:57.430
The first bag of blood was placed down, and
the taint team was met with the voice of SCP-5633.

00:14:57.430 --> 00:15:01.560
“I LIKE TO LIE.”

00:15:01.560 --> 00:15:05.730
The taint team was perplexed as the bag began
to be drained of blood.

00:15:05.730 --> 00:15:09.060
What did SCP-5633 lie about?

00:15:09.060 --> 00:15:12.890
Another bag was placed on the ground and Firestarter
was commanded to wait.

00:15:12.890 --> 00:15:14.290
“MY CREATION WAS ALWAYS INHERENT.

00:15:14.290 --> 00:15:16.650
YOUR ASSISTANCE WAS NEVER NECESSARY.

00:15:16.650 --> 00:15:25.680
I TOLD YOU IF YOU HELPED ME YOU WOULD BE SAVED.”

00:15:25.680 --> 00:15:30.760
Doctor Henry, in a fit of confusion and rage,
threw the rest of the bags to the ground.

00:15:30.760 --> 00:15:32.580
The only response he was given.

00:15:32.580 --> 00:15:36.510
“I AM LYING TO YOU.”

00:15:36.510 --> 00:15:40.279
Suddenly, the Hume levels in the room spiked
to 4000.

00:15:40.279 --> 00:15:45.620
The room changed appearance again, now, the
taint team was almost drowning in SCP-5633’s

00:15:45.620 --> 00:15:46.900
liquid.

00:15:46.900 --> 00:15:51.680
They tried to scream but were only met with
mouthfuls of the disgusting black and red

00:15:51.680 --> 00:15:52.680
mixture.

00:15:52.680 --> 00:15:54.990
As fast as the liquid appeared, it was gone.

00:15:54.990 --> 00:15:56.970
And so was the team.

00:15:56.970 --> 00:16:01.200
There was nothing but silence and the soft
sound of slithering.

00:16:01.200 --> 00:16:04.829
Personnel at Site 202 realized about one hour
later that something must have gone wrong

00:16:04.829 --> 00:16:09.850
with this investigation, and hastily traveled
to SCP-5633.

00:16:09.850 --> 00:16:14.420
Over 50 members of various Mobile Task Forces
and security teams entered the school and

00:16:14.420 --> 00:16:20.170
its basement, only to be met with the disgustingly
cruel fate of the taint team.

00:16:20.170 --> 00:16:24.210
SCP-5633 had reached a height of almost 20
feet.

00:16:24.210 --> 00:16:28.120
Doctor Henry’s left arm and nose were seen
floating in the middle of this mass.

00:16:28.120 --> 00:16:31.800
Half of Agent Firestarter’s face was seen
jutting out of what appeared to be the shoulder

00:16:31.800 --> 00:16:32.800
of SCP-5633.

00:16:32.800 --> 00:16:38.519
The legs of Researcher Zeissman were found
at the lower portion of the entity, laying

00:16:38.519 --> 00:16:41.380
completely still other than random twitching.

00:16:41.380 --> 00:16:45.180
The head of Director Strysand was peeking
out of the top of SCP-5633.

00:16:45.180 --> 00:16:51.730
Her eyes had been completely replaced with
SCP-5633’s veins, and she appeared to be

00:16:51.730 --> 00:16:54.100
crying the liquid constantly.

00:16:54.100 --> 00:16:59.350
It seemed that SCP-5633 had been influencing
events from the beginning, from the death

00:16:59.350 --> 00:17:05.539
of Doctor Olich to the pipe explosion to possibly
even creating the entire narrative of being

00:17:05.539 --> 00:17:09.689
kicked out of another universe by an alternate
Foundation.

00:17:09.689 --> 00:17:16.030
The SCP Foundation does know one thing for
sure though, SCP-5633 requires a great amount

00:17:16.030 --> 00:17:21.169
of blood, and it just so happens, human beings
have a lot for it.

00:17:21.169 --> 00:17:26.579
Now go check out “SCP-354 - The Red Pool”
and “Frightening Lost Ronald Reagan VHS

00:17:26.579 --> 00:17:35.429
Tape You Must Watch - SCP-1981 &amp; SCP-095”
for more blood-curdling SCPs from SCP Explained!

